  ],
  "events": [
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "timestamp": 13,
      "actor": "unknown",
      "action": "speak",
      "data": {
        "text": "\u201cI witnessed the First Stars weep metals into the void. I cooled my essence in the accretion disks of orphaned worlds. I knew the Wise Ones when they were but frantic, chemical whispers in tidal pools, and I watched them ascend, and then\u2026 diminish. I have seen galaxies collide, black holes sing their hunger-songs, and life\u2014fragile, stubborn, magnificent life\u2014ignite on a thousand million rocks. I was ancient when the dragons first carved their territories from nebular dust. The wars that wrack your histories are but the last, fading echoes of conflicts I saw dawn and die before your world had a crust.\u201d",
        "line": 20
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "timestamp": 25,
      "actor": "unknown",
      "action": "speak",
      "data": {
        "text": "\u201cI have been father, custodian, and historian to this entire celestial house,\u201d",
        "line": 36
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "timestamp": 57,
      "actor": "unknown",
      "action": "speak",
      "data": {
        "text": "\u201cLittle ember,\u201d",
        "line": 81
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "timestamp": 112,
      "actor": "unknown",
      "action": "speak",
      "data": {
        "text": "\u201cThe Bronze Dragon is wounded, little ember. It calls from the dust clouds of Orion. It cannot hold the Solar Lineage. My essence must go. To mend. To\u2026 father.\u201d",
        "line": 152
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "timestamp": 118,
      "actor": "unknown",
      "action": "speak",
      "data": {
        "text": "\u201cWatch for my son,\u201d",
        "line": 160
      }
    }
  ],
